Chamfers and fillets: a closed rim whose analytic blend leaves its face
over a cut-out along a whole edge of the rim, the gap running from the
only piece of another edge round to that piece's start (mitcad#343).

The case: a bore's rim of radius 85 in two arcs is chamfered 1 on the top
and 2 down the wall. A pocket from below, a cylinder whose side breaks
through the wall, ends 1 below the top, so along the shorter arc the wall
is a strip only 1 high over the pocket's ceiling; the arcs' vertices lie
where the pocket's side meets the wall. The chamfer's contact 2 down the
wall lies in the pocket all along the shorter arc: SplitKPart gives the
longer arc one piece, its ends on the pocket's side, and the shorter arc
none. ChFi3d_FillKPartRoundGapsAcrossEdges (the faces round from the
pocket's side back to it cut the blend over the gap: the side, the
ceiling, the side) looked for the next edge with pieces only among the
other edges, never back at the gap's own first edge, so the gap was left
to the walk that chamfers do not have, and the chamfer failed. The bodies
stored in the files cut the chamfer's cone lengthwise by the ceiling,
which keeps its part outside the cone (up to 84.5 from the axis), and near
the arc's ends by the pocket's side, both growing up to the cut.

- ChFi3d_FillKPartRoundGapsAcrossEdges: on a closed spine whose other
  edges have no piece, the search for the edge where the contact comes
  back goes round to the first edge again, a period on (the gap's last
  edge may be its first; A and C, the pieces before and after the gap,
  may be one piece). The edges of the gap are told apart by their place
  in it, not by their numbers: the first one's range starts at A's end,
  the last one's ends at C's start, and an edge before the first one or
  the first one again lies a period on.

On the design's body before the item: valid, every face on the stored
body's within 2e-6 mm both ways, the change of volume -522.6458 against
the file's -522.6452 mm3; before, the chamfer failed. Synthetic: a disc's
rim in two arcs, split where a pocket from below breaks through its wall
1 under the top, chamfered 1 by 2, either arc first, the seam at either
corner: valid, the material taken within 1e-6 of the section's revolved
part inside the body, the ceiling cut back to 84.5; before, the chamfer
failed.

Upstream: new.
